          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What does osteoarthritis guidance describe as core treatment before anything else?",
          "answer": "The core treatment guidance for osteoarthritis emphasizes non-pharmacologic management as the first step. Specifically, structured exercise is strongly recommended, as it carries substantial evidence for effectiveness in managing knee and hip osteoarthritis. This exercise program should include muscle strengthening, range of movement activities, and aerobic workouts, ideally supervised initially to ensure proper adherence and progression. Importantly, exercise can be beneficial regardless of the severity of joint damage, age, or initial pain level. Pain during exercise, as long as it remains tolerable, is not seen as a sign of damage (source: Rheumatology and orthopedic society guidance).\n\nI did not cover specific medications or other potential treatments, as the focus was on core non-pharmacologic approaches.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
